The regular expression uses a named capture group, `all`, so `mask_card` can be called both from a direct string replace and from the depth-first walk above. If you need the function to be faster on very large payloads, move the compiled pattern outside the function. Do not forget that this code is for masking during analysis and doesn't substitute for rotating or offloading card data that is already stored.

